# Edge Agent Scanner

Static analysis CLI for local agent repositories. Emits a versioned `report.json` for later integration with the Edge Agent AI UI.

## Install (editable)

Use a virtual environment (recommended on macOS / PEP 668 systems). From the `scanner/` directory:

```bash
python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate   # Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -e ".[dev]"
```

## Run tests

With the venv activated:

```bash
pytest -q
```

## Scan a repository

```bash
python -m edge_agent_scanner.cli scan /path/to/repo --out report.json
```

`--out` defaults to `./report.json` if omitted.

Scanned text extensions include `.py`, `.ts`, `.tsx`, `.js`, `.jsx`, `.json`, `.yaml`, `.yml`, `.md`, `.txt`, and `.toml` (for `pyproject.toml` / manifest parsing).

## Report schema

See `edge_agent_scanner/report.py` for the Pydantic models. Findings use `rule_id` values aligned with the UI Scan Center check IDs.
